  "implementation_findings": [
    "Matrix producer lowering emits row/column extent statements and a coefficient function; it returns a Matrix descriptor carrying dimensions, coefficient identity and transpose orientation, rather than numeric entries.",
    "Multiplication lowering consumes this descriptor and emits matrix/apply or matrix/apply-transpose with vector shape checks, dimensions and coefficient. The descriptor does not create an eager matrix value.",
    "At runtime, op35/op36 allocate only an output vector and invoke the native matrix kernel over input columns/output row slices. The producer coefficient arithmetic participates in these products; it is not replaced with an embedded 5500-by-5500 array.",
    "At sequence iteration invocation, captured dimension values are copied into the callable Context alongside explicit current x. The surrounding-scope A dependency is therefore represented with implicit dimension captures; coefficient(i,j) itself has no free captures.",
    "Consequently there is no matrix A data initialization stage to place outside the measured process. Runtime input determines dimensions; generated arithmetic executes while processing each vector. Compile time prepares code and descriptor representation, not coefficient values for the full input."
  ]
